              <div class="sp-steer-head">
                <span class="sp-steer-title">Steering mode &mdash; induced dipole profile</span>
                <span class="sp-steer-sub" id="sp-steer-sub">&xi; = 0</span>
              </div>
              <div class="chart-wrap sp-steer-wrap"><canvas id="sp-steer-chart" aria-label="Induced dipole magnitude vs array index for the steering mode"></canvas></div>
            </div>

            <div class="notes-card card" id="sp-notes">
              <h4>Notes</h4>
              <p>
                <strong>Generalized Smith&ndash;Purcell.</strong>
                A swift electron (v/c, energy K) flies parallel to a periodic array of N point
                emitters (period a, impact parameter b) and induces a coherent dipole on each.
                Each Fourier mode &#8467; of the (engineered) dipole profile opens an emission
                channel at
                sin&thinsp;&theta;<sub>n,&#8467;</sub>&nbsp;=&nbsp;1/&beta;&nbsp;&minus;&nbsp;(n&nbsp;&minus;&nbsp;&#8467;/N)&thinsp;&lambda;/a (Eq.&nbsp;6);
                &#8467;&nbsp;=&nbsp;0 is the ordinary Smith&ndash;Purcell line. Steering &xi; modulates
                |p<sub>j</sub>|&thinsp;=&thinsp;1&nbsp;+&nbsp;sin(2&pi;&xi;j/N) to select channel &#8467;&nbsp;=&nbsp;&xi;.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Polarization.</strong> The electron field drives an elliptical dipole
                d&nbsp;=&nbsp;(i/&gamma;)K<sub>0</sub>&thinsp;x&#770;&nbsp;+&nbsp;K<sub>1</sub>&thinsp;z&#770; (Eq.&nbsp;9): the i makes
                x and z oscillate 90&deg; out of phase. In the &phi;&nbsp;=&nbsp;0 plane the emission is
                purely p-polarized; off-plane (&phi;&nbsp;&ne;&nbsp;0) it becomes elliptical, with
                wavelength- and angle-dependent handedness (Stokes S<sub>3</sub>).
              </p>
              <div class="sp-examples">
                <button type="button" class="sp-example" id="sp-ex-1" aria-pressed="false">
                  <span class="sp-example__head">Example 1 &mdash; SP dispersion</span>
                  <span class="sp-example__params">K&nbsp;=&nbsp;30&nbsp;keV (v/c&nbsp;=&nbsp;0.328) &middot; a&nbsp;=&nbsp;300&nbsp;nm &middot; b&nbsp;=&nbsp;10&nbsp;nm &middot; N&nbsp;=&nbsp;11 &middot; &xi;&nbsp;=&nbsp;0 &middot; dipole&nbsp;&#8741;&nbsp;x (parallel) &middot; E&nbsp;=&nbsp;3.2&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;1.65&nbsp;eV &middot; &theta;&nbsp;=&nbsp;&minus;180&hellip;&minus;55&deg;</span>
                  <span class="sp-example__hint">Click to load these parameters and show the spectral-dependence map &rarr;</span>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

